   1636  fc4c							; Room-exit handlers — MOVED from bank0 (C3, 2026-10-20; were $F4DB-$F535 = 90 B).
   1637  fc4c							; C1 (2026-10-20): LEVEL_FORMAT 2 — there is NO connection table any more. Each
   1638  fc4c							; room owns ONE grid-position byte (x<<4|y, normalised to the level origin) at
   1639  fc4c							; level base + n (C2 2026-10-20: the 3 B record is three columns, so the
   1640  fc4c							; position column still starts one block-of-n in), and an exit is resolved by
   1641  fc4c							; stepping that byte by a direction delta ($FF up / $01 down / $F0 left /
   1642  fc4c							; $10 right) and SCANNING the level's position column for a match (<= 20
   1643  fc4c							; iterations, cold path = room load only).
   1644  fc4c							;
   1645  fc4c							; Why no boundary guard is needed: a nibble of 15 never occurs in a stored
   1646  fc4c							; position (POSITION_SPAN = 15 in convert_level.py, nibble 15 = sentinel), and
   1647  fc4c							; stepping off the grid always wraps the moved nibble to 15 — so an exit past
   1648  fc4c							; the grid edge can never match a room. The old nibble-room-index pack capped a
   1649  fc4c							; level at 15 rooms; this lifts it to 225 grid cells (20 rooms/level with room
   1650  fc4c							; to spare) at 1 B/room instead of 2.
   1651  fc4c							;
   1652  fc4c							; Entry: bank0's `jsr ExitRoomXxx` pad ($FBD9-$FBE4, `sta $1FF8`) -> the `jmp`
   1653  fc4c							; halves at $FBDC-$FBE5 above. Every exit path ends in a `jmp`:
   1654  fc4c							;   * no exit	    -> ReturnPad (bank0 `rts` pops the caller's jsr frame)
   1655  fc4c							;   * room changed -> `jmp EnterRoomB2`, whose own `jmp ReturnPad` does the same
   1656  fc4c							; The opposite-edge placement is written BEFORE EnterRoomB2 because EnterRoom
   1657  fc4c							; never reads/writes RoomX/RoomY (verified in EnterRoomB2 + B3RoomBlocks), and
   1658  fc4c							; Y is used for the constant so A keeps the ROOM INDEX EnterRoomB2 stores.
   1659  fc4c							; Guard: verify_build.check_exit_handlers.
   1660  fc4c							; ==============================================================================
   1661  fc4c		       00 00 00 	      .ds	$FC4F - *, 0
